('node-11-10', 'phase-11-lesson-10-high-performance-allocators-jemalloc-tcma', 'module-12', 10, 'Lesson 12.10: High-Performance Allocators: jemalloc, tcmalloc & Mimalloc', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 11.7, Phase 0', 'Prerequisites: Lesson 11.7, Phase 0 | Subtopics: 6 items', 'Systems project application', 320, 12, 2810.0, 500.0, '# Lesson 11.10: High-Performance Allocators: jemalloc, tcmalloc & Mimalloc

- **Status**: `[State: Active | Complete Specification | Core]`
- **Prerequisites**: Lesson 11.7, Phase 0
- **Subtopics**:
  - `11.10.1` Standard system allocators (glibc ptmalloc) limitations: lock contention on multi-threaded workloads, severe memory fragmentation
  - `11.10.2` jemalloc architecture: thread-specific caches (tcache), arenas, size classes (small, large, huge), and proactive dirty page purging
  - `11.10.3` tcmalloc (Google Thread-Caching Malloc): thread caches, central cache, page heap, and lock-free thread allocation paths
  - `11.10.4` Memory fragmentation mechanics: internal fragmentation (slack space in size class) vs external fragmentation (unusable scattered holes)
  - `11.10.5` Dropping in alternative allocators: setting `LD_PRELOAD=/usr/lib/libjemalloc.so` without recompiling application binaries
  - `11.10.6` Runtime profiling with jemalloc: enabling heap profiling via `MALLOC_CONF=prof:true` and analyzing memory dumps with `jeprof`
- **Key Failure Modes & Edge Cases**: Severe glibc allocator memory fragmentation causing 10GB RSS usage when the application only holds 2GB of actual live data.
- **Verification & Mastery Check**: Benchmark glibc ptmalloc vs jemalloc on a high-concurrency multi-threaded workload; measure RSS reduction and throughput improvement.
- **Project Application**: ModelPulse: High-performance memory allocator benchmark.', '{"solution.py": "# Phase 11 // Lesson 11.10: High-Performance Allocators: jemalloc, tcmalloc & Mimalloc\n\ndef solve():\n    \"\"\"\n    Verification: Benchmark glibc ptmalloc vs jemalloc on a high-concurrency multi-threaded workload; measure RSS redu\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n"}'::jsonb, '{"lesson": "11.10", "subtopics_count": 6, "verification_criteria": "Benchmark glibc ptmalloc vs jemalloc on a high-concurrency multi-threaded workload; measure RSS reduction and throughput improvement.", "subtopics": ["11.10.1 Standard system allocators (glibc ptmalloc) limitations: lock contention on multi-threaded workloads, severe memory fragmentation", "11.10.2 jemalloc architecture: thread-specific caches (tcache), arenas, size classes (small, large, huge), and proactive dirty page purging", "11.10.3 tcmalloc (Google Thread-Caching Malloc): thread caches, central cache, page heap, and lock-free thread allocation paths", "11.10.4 Memory fragmentation mechanics: internal fragmentation (slack space in size class) vs external fragmentation (unusable scattered holes)", "11.10.5 Dropping in alternative allocators: setting `LD_PRELOAD=/usr/lib/libjemalloc.so` without recompiling application binaries", "11.10.6 Runtime profiling with jemalloc: enabling heap profiling via `MALLOC_CONF=prof:true` and analyzing memory dumps with `jeprof`"]}'::jsonb, '["Explain how this implementation prevents: Severe glibc allocator memory fragmentation causing 10GB RSS usage when the application only holds 2GB of actual live da", "How does High-Performance Allocators: jemalloc, tcmalloc & Mimalloc scale under memory and concurrency constraints?", "Defend the architectural tradeoffs of this design in production."]'::jsonb),
('node-11-11', 'phase-11-lesson-11-memory-leak-debugging-in-native-code-valg', 'module-12', 11, 'Lesson 12.11: Memory Leak Debugging in Native Code: Valgrind, ASan & LeakSanitizer', 'Prerequisites: Phase 0, Lesson 11.9', 'Prerequisites: Phase 0, Lesson 11.9 | Subtopics: 6 items', 'Systems project application', 320, 12, 2870.0, 550.0, '# Lesson 11.11: Memory Leak Debugging in Native Code: Valgrind, ASan & LeakSanitizer

